  "slug": "environment-shape-regulatory-variation-1c31",
  "summary": "Preprints link graph pangenomes, mapping strategy and TE insertions to trait and expression interpretation across plant and fungal genomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that interpretation of genotype, expression and trait data depends on the quality and structure of the reference. In Capsicum, a graph pangenome anchors k-mer GWAS signals for pungency and aroma terpene traits to Pun1 haplotypes and TPS genes. A six-species comparison of TopHat2, HISAT2 and STAR reports genome-guided mapping errors for tandemly duplicated genes. In six bread wheat cultivars, cultivar-specific TE insertions in gene bodies track homoeolog expression bias, mainly through suppression. The Rhizoctonia solani AG1-IB assembly resolves haplotypes of a heterokaryotic pathogen, with ~97.75% identity between them. Tipularia discolor shows candidate gene mining on a fragmented assembly, and MEAM-OWL adds browser-based motif enrichment tied to expression. New here is the use of pangenome and haplotype-resolved frameworks to localize variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
